<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hujung Galuh</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hujung Galuh was a port on the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brantas-river">Brantas River</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-java">East Java</a>, mentioned in inscriptions of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/airlangga">Airlangga</a> in the 11th century. Airlangga built dams on the Brantas to protect it from floods, and it served as a harbour where ships from other islands and overseas traded. Its exact location is uncertain but it is generally placed near modern Surabaya.</p></div>
